#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 0. Setup {#step-0-setup}"
msgstr "Langkah 0. Persediaan {#step-0-setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, import the packages and functions needed to run this notebook "
"successfully.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, import pakej dan fungsi yang diperlukan untuk menjalankan notebook "
"ini dengan berjaya.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1. Map the problem {#step-1-map-the-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1. Petakan masalah {#step-1-map-the-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For ease of demonstration, we select a 1D mirror Ising chain. The 1D Ising "
"chain gives a nicely dense circuit structure, which is convenient for "
"showcasing PEC implementations. A mirror circuit makes it straightforward to"
" know the expected outcome (namely, we should measure an observable of 1).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kemudahan demonstrasi, kami memilih rantai Ising cermin 1D. Rantai "
"Ising 1D memberikan struktur litar yang padat dan bagus, yang memudahkan "
"untuk mempamerkan pelaksanaan PEC. litar cermin memudahkan kita mengetahui "
"hasil yang dijangkakan (iaitu, kita sepatutnya mengukur observable sebesar "
"1).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Further, we want to run a mirror circuit, so for every gate in the second "
"half of the circuit, there needs to be an inverse gate in the first half. As"
" the measured observable **$<X_6 Z_{13}>$** has non-Z-basis measurements, "
"and the executor accounts for the desired basis at the end of the circuit, "
"we provide a `prepare_basis` function that inserts the appropriate gates at "
"the start of the mirror circuit. This detail is specific to our mirror-"
"circuit demonstration. The `get_measurement_bases` function allows us to "
"easily identify which gates are needed and where to append them, as well as "
"keeping track of qubit index subtleties arising from conventions in `box` "
"annotation as discussed in the \"Prepare canonical bases measurements\" "
"section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, kami ingin menjalankan litar cermin, jadi untuk setiap gate "
"dalam separuh kedua litar, perlu ada gate songsang dalam separuh pertama. "
"Memandangkan observable yang diukur **$<X_6 Z_{13}>$** mempunyai pengukuran "
"bukan asas-Z, dan Executor mengambil kira asas yang dikehendaki pada "
"penghujung litar, kami menyediakan fungsi `prepare_basis` yang memasukkan "
"gate yang sesuai pada permulaan litar cermin. Butiran ini khusus untuk "
"demonstrasi litar cermin kami. Fungsi `get_measurement_bases` membolehkan "
"kami mengenal pasti dengan mudah gate yang diperlukan dan di mana perlu "
"menambahkannya, serta menjejaki kehalusan indeks qubit yang timbul daripada "
"konvensyen dalam anotasi `box` seperti yang dibincangkan dalam bahagian "
"\"Sediakan pengukuran asas kanonikal\".\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2. Optimize {#step-2-optimize}"
msgstr "Langkah 2. Optimumkan {#step-2-optimize}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will optimize details associated with the circuit to be run, the "
"observable to be measured, and the noise-learning parameters. As a starting "
"point, we ensure that we instantiate a backend with fractional gates turned "
"on as an option. These fractional gates will allow for greater sensitivity "
"in some of our post-selection filtering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan optimumkan butiran berkaitan dengan litar yang hendak dijalankan, "
"observable yang hendak diukur, dan parameter pembelajaran hingar. Sebagai "
"titik permulaan, kita pastikan backend dinyatakan dengan fractional gates "
"dihidupkan sebagai pilihan. Fractional gates ini membolehkan kepekaan yang "
"lebih tinggi dalam beberapa penapisan pasca-pemilihan kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we will transpile our circuit to ISA instructions, [as required for "
"execution on our QPUs](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/isa-circuits). For "
"the data collected in this experiment, we hand select our qubits based on "
"evaluation of the highest quality chain.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita akan transpil litar kita kepada arahan ISA, [seperti yang "
"diperlukan untuk pelaksanaan pada QPU "
"kita](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/isa-circuits). Untuk data yang "
"dikumpul dalam eksperimen ini, kita pilih sendiri qubit kita berdasarkan "
"penilaian rantai berkualiti tertinggi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_2.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_2.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Box the circuit {#box-the-circuit}"
msgstr "Kotak litar tersebut {#box-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For ease of implementation, we will utilize the "
"`generate_boxing_pass_manager` transpilation pass, which places the circuit "
"instructions into annotated boxes. These boxes clearly indicate where, in "
"the case of PEC, antinoise should be injected into the circuit. For details "
"on settings, refer to the [Samplomatic "
"documentation.](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/)\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kemudahan pelaksanaan, kita akan gunakan laluan transpilasi "
"`generate_boxing_pass_manager`, yang meletakkan arahan litar ke dalam kotak "
"beranotasi. Kotak-kotak ini menunjukkan dengan jelas di mana, dalam kes PEC,"
" antinoise perlu disuntik ke dalam litar. Untuk butiran tetapan, rujuk "
"[dokumentasi Samplomatic.](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the SLC workflow the use of "
"`inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` later in the process "
"because this allows us to  uniquely identify each `BoxOp` in the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu diambil perhatian bahawa aliran kerja SLC menggunakan "
"`inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` kemudian dalam proses "
"kerana ini membolehkan kita mengenal pasti setiap `BoxOp` dalam litar secara"
" unik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `find_unique_box_instructions` function iterates through the provided "
"boxed circuit and identifies those that have unique 2Q layers or "
"measurements, for the purpose of noise learning and noise injection.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `find_unique_box_instructions` mengulangi litar berkotak yang "
"diberikan dan mengenal pasti yang mempunyai lapisan 2Q unik atau pengukuran,"
" bagi tujuan pembelajaran hingar dan suntikan hingar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_3.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_3.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare canonical bases measurements {#prepare-canonical-bases-measurements}"
msgstr ""
"Sediakan pengukuran asas kanonik {#prepare-canonical-bases-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Due to how the qubits are labeled when identifying unique 2Q layers, one "
"must take special care to keep track of qubit ordering. Below, we introduce "
"the notion of `canonical_qubits` as a means to appropriately update the "
"qubit ordering when providing it to the executor, as a result of how qubit "
"order is captured when boxing circuits and finding unique instructions. See "
"the [Qubit ordering "
"convention](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-"
"ordering-convention) documentation for details.\n"
msgstr ""
"Disebabkan cara qubit dilabel semasa mengenal pasti lapisan 2Q unik, "
"seseorang perlu berhati-hati untuk menjejaki susunan qubit. Di bawah, kita "
"perkenalkan konsep `canonical_qubits` sebagai cara untuk mengemas kini "
"susunan qubit dengan sewajarnya apabila memberikannya kepada executor, hasil"
" daripada bagaimana susunan qubit ditangkap semasa mempetak litar dan "
"mencari arahan unik. Lihat dokumentasi [Konvensyen susunan "
"qubit](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-"
"ordering-convention) untuk butiran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Workflow for lightcone shading, noise learning, and anti-noise injection "
"{#workflow-for-lightcone-shading-noise-learning-and-anti-noise-injection-1}"
msgstr ""
"Alur kerja untuk pembayang kon cahaya, pembelajaran hingar, dan suntikan "
"anti-hingar {#workflow-for-lightcone-shading-noise-learning-and-anti-noise-"
"injection-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Note**: For the implementation of SLC-PEC in this tutorial, we run SLC "
"bound computations **before** the noise learning has been completed, so the "
"to-be-mitigated circuit is run as close in time as possible to the learned "
"noise model. In principle, this workflow can be further enhanced to execute "
"simultaneously.  Namely, a noise-learning job is run while, in parallel, "
"noise bounds are estimated. For an arbitrary quantum circuit, the noise-"
"bound computation can scale with a weakly exponential dependence.  As such, "
"it might be prudent to use parallelized execution when trying to maximize "
"the workflow's efficiency. To this end, we briefly demonstrate this by "
"including cluster-based (128-thread) resources and showing how you can "
"achieve a more refined set of bounds for a provided circuit when constrained"
" to equal computation-time limits, compared to our laptop (8 threads). "
"Furthermore, although not implemented in this workflow, you can parallelize "
"the QPU executions for noise learning and noise-bound computations to "
"achieve the most efficient workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"> **Nota**: Bagi pelaksanaan SLC-PEC dalam tutorial ini, kita menjalankan "
"pengiraan sempadan SLC **sebelum** pembelajaran hingar selesai, supaya litar"
" yang hendak dikurangkan hingarnya dijalankan sedekat mungkin dari segi masa"
" dengan model hingar yang dipelajari. Secara prinsipnya, alur kerja ini "
"boleh ditingkatkan lagi untuk dilaksanakan secara serentak. Iaitu, kerja "
"pembelajaran hingar dijalankan sambil, secara selari, sempadan hingar "
"dianggarkan. Bagi litar kuantum yang sewenang-wenangnya, pengiraan sempadan "
"hingar boleh berskala dengan pergantungan eksponen yang lemah. Oleh itu, "
"mungkin bijak untuk menggunakan pelaksanaan selari apabila cuba "
"memaksimumkan kecekapan alur kerja. Untuk tujuan ini, kita menunjukkan ini "
"secara ringkas dengan memasukkan sumber berasaskan kluster (128 benang) dan "
"menunjukkan cara untuk mendapatkan set sempadan yang lebih halus bagi litar "
"yang diberikan apabila terhad kepada had masa pengiraan yang sama, "
"berbanding komputer riba kita (8 benang). Tambahan pula, walaupun tidak "
"dilaksanakan dalam alur kerja ini, anda boleh menyejajarkan pelaksanaan QPU "
"untuk pembelajaran hingar dan pengiraan sempadan hingar bagi mencapai alur "
"kerja yang paling cekap.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Predict to-be-learned noise-model Paulis {#predict-to-be-learned-noise-"
"model-paulis}"
msgstr ""
"Ramal Pauli model hingar yang akan dipelajari {#predict-to-be-learned-noise-"
"model-paulis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `generate_noise_model_paulis` function goes through each boxed layer of "
"the provided circuit and generates all relevant weight-one and weight-two "
"Pauli terms, taking into account the circuit's qubit connectivity, and "
"selecting terms that are relevant to the active nodes and edges. These terms"
" are then used to compute forward and backward noise bounds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `generate_noise_model_paulis` melalui setiap lapisan berpetak dalam "
"litar yang diberikan dan menghasilkan semua sebutan Pauli berat-satu dan "
"berat-dua yang relevan, dengan mengambil kira keterhubungan qubit litar, dan"
" memilih sebutan yang relevan dengan nod dan tepi yang aktif. Sebutan-"
"sebutan ini kemudiannya digunakan untuk mengira sempadan hingar ke hadapan "
"dan ke belakang.\n"

#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"a. Compute and tighten forward bounds {#a-compute-and-tighten-forward-"
"bounds}"
msgstr ""
"a. Kira dan ketatkan sempadan ke hadapan {#a-compute-and-tighten-forward-"
"bounds}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `compute_forward_bounds` function evaluates the commutation relations "
"between the gates in each layer and the above-generated Pauli terms in terms"
" of how forward-propagation errors affect the desired observable $A$. For "
"gates that commute with the Pauli terms, nothing is done. For Clifford "
"gates, they are pushed toward the beginning of the circuit. For non-Clifford"
" gates, we approximate their influence on the target observables to later be"
" prioritized for noise cancelation (after all bounds have been merged). This"
" bound is achieved by first applying the L2 norm (namely, the square root of"
" the sum of squares of the relevant Pauli-term coefficients). When there are"
" too many qubit terms involved, we revert to a looser bound that uses the "
"triangle inequality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `compute_forward_bounds` menilai hubungan komutasi antara get dalam "
"setiap lapisan dan sebutan Pauli yang dihasilkan di atas dari segi bagaimana"
" ralat perambatan ke hadapan mempengaruhi observable yang dikehendaki $A$. "
"Untuk get yang berkomut dengan sebutan Pauli, tiada apa yang dilakukan. "
"Untuk get Clifford, ia ditolak ke arah permulaan litar. Untuk get bukan "
"Clifford, kita menganggarkan pengaruhnya terhadap observable sasaran untuk "
"kemudiannya diprioritikan bagi pembatalan hingar (selepas semua sempadan "
"digabungkan). Sempadan ini dicapai dengan terlebih dahulu menggunakan norma "
"L2 (iaitu, punca kuasa dua bagi jumlah kuasa dua pekali sebutan Pauli yang "
"relevan). Apabila terlalu banyak sebutan qubit terlibat, kita bertukar "
"kepada sempadan yang lebih longgar menggunakan ketaksamaan segitiga.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Laptop-level resources {#laptop-level-resources}"
msgstr "Sumber peringkat komputer riba {#laptop-level-resources}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection}"
msgstr ""
"Visualkan SLC untuk pemeriksaan manual {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can interpret the behavior of the shaded bounds by examining how the "
"measurements and Pauli terms interact with the local errors. These patterns "
"are characteristic of this kicked Ising Hamiltonian time-evolution problem "
"and also appear in the paper [Lightcone Shading for Classically Accelerated "
"Quantum Error Mitigation](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.04401), with several "
"telltale features:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu boleh mentafsir tingkah laku sempadan berlorek dengan memeriksa "
"bagaimana pengukuran dan sebutan Pauli berinteraksi dengan ralat tempatan. "
"Corak-corak ini adalah ciri bagi masalah evolusi masa Hamiltonian Ising "
"tertendang ini dan juga muncul dalam kertas kerja [Lightcone Shading for "
"Classically Accelerated Quantum Error "
"Mitigation](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.04401), dengan beberapa ciri yang "
"ketara:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can clearly distinguish the two cones arising from the two non-identity "
"Paulis in the observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat membezakan dengan jelas dua kon yang timbul daripada dua Pauli "
"bukan identiti dalam observable.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can see that the X measurement on qubit 6 commutes with the X error in "
"the rightmost layer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat melihat bahawa pengukuran X pada qubit 6 berkomut dengan ralat X "
"dalam lapisan paling kanan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can see that the Z Pauli on qubit 13 commutes with the Z error in the "
"rightmost layer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat melihat bahawa Pauli Z pada qubit 13 berkomut dengan ralat Z "
"dalam lapisan paling kanan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we reach the timeout specified above, the remaining layers to the left "
"are filled entirely with trivial bounds of two.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila kita mencapai tamat masa yang dinyatakan di atas, lapisan-lapisan "
"yang tersisa di sebelah kiri diisi sepenuhnya dengan sempadan remeh bernilai"
" dua.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_4.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_4.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_5.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_5.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_6.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_6.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"b. Compute and tighten forward bounds {#b-compute-and-tighten-forward-"
"bounds}"
msgstr ""
"b. Kira dan ketatkan sempadan ke hadapan {#b-compute-and-tighten-forward-"
"bounds}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We next tighten the bounds by using the `tighten_with_speed_limit` function,"
" which tracks how the observable spreads backward through the circuit and "
"uses that spread to place upper bounds on the effect of each noise operator,"
" taking the smaller of the forward bound just computed, and the backward-"
"propagation bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya kita mengetatkan sempadan dengan menggunakan fungsi "
"`tighten_with_speed_limit`, yang menjejaki cara observable merebak ke "
"belakang melalui litar dan menggunakan rebakan tersebut untuk menetapkan had"
" atas pada kesan setiap pengendali hingar, mengambil nilai yang lebih kecil "
"antara sempadan ke hadapan yang baru dikira, dan sempadan perambatan ke "
"belakang.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection-1}"
msgstr ""
"Visualkan SLC untuk pemeriksaan manual {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can further tighten the bounds by accounting for lightcone limitation. In"
" principle, this gives us a smoother transition from the computed bounds to "
"the trivial bounds set forth after the timeout was reached. Here, the effect"
" is not as visible because the lightcones have already reached the edge of "
"the circuit. \n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh mengetatkan lagi sempadan dengan mengambil kira had kon cahaya. "
"Secara prinsipnya, ini memberikan kita peralihan yang lebih lancar daripada "
"sempadan yang dikira kepada sempadan remeh yang ditetapkan selepas tamat "
"masa tercapai. Di sini, kesannya tidak begitu ketara kerana kon cahaya sudah"
" mencapai tepi litar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_7.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_7.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_8.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_8.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_9.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_9.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "c. Compute backward bounds {#c-compute-backward-bounds}"
msgstr "c. Kira sempadan ke belakang {#c-compute-backward-bounds}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This part of noise prediction evaluates how an error at a particular layer "
"can affect the input state $\\rho$. The `compute_backward_bounds` function "
"first inverts the circuit, removes measurement gates, and then proceeds with"
" a similar analysis as was done for the forward-bound computations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahagian ramalan hingar ini menilai bagaimana ralat pada lapisan tertentu "
"boleh mempengaruhi keadaan input $\\rho$. Fungsi `compute_backward_bounds` "
"terlebih dahulu menyongsangkan litar, membuang get pengukuran, kemudian "
"meneruskan dengan analisis yang serupa seperti yang dilakukan untuk "
"pengiraan sempadan ke hadapan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection-2}"
msgstr ""
"Visualkan SLC untuk pemeriksaan manual {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From computing backward bounds, we can see how the initial state structure "
"governs the early behavior of error propagation:\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada pengiraan sempadan ke belakang, kita dapat melihat bagaimana "
"struktur keadaan awal mengawal tingkah laku awal perambatan ralat:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can clearly see how the Z errors initially commute with the |0⟩ initial "
"state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat melihat dengan jelas bagaimana ralat Z pada mulanya berkomut "
"dengan keadaan awal |0⟩.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only on qubit 6, where we initialize the +1 eigenstate of the X basis, does "
"a Z error fail to commute, while an X error does commute.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hanya pada qubit 6, di mana kita menginisialisasi eigenstate +1 bagi asas X,"
" ralat Z gagal berkomut, manakala ralat X berkomut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_10.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_10.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_11.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_11.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_12.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah litar kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/slc/01-getting-"
"started/output_12.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Preview merged bounds without learned noise rates {#preview-merged-bounds-"
"without-learned-noise-rates}"
msgstr ""
"Pratonton sempadan yang digabungkan tanpa kadar hingar yang dipelajari "
"{#preview-merged-bounds-without-learned-noise-rates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `merged_bounds` function determines the point in the circuit where "
"switching from backward bounds to forward bounds minimizes the total "
"estimated bias on the desired observable. This bias is computed as the sum "
"of the backward-bound contributions for all noise locations before that "
"point, plus the forward-bound contributions for all noise locations after "
"it. Currently, this is done uniformly for all qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `merged_bounds` menentukan titik dalam litar di mana peralihan "
"daripada sempadan ke belakang kepada sempadan ke hadapan meminimumkan jumlah"
" anggaran pincang pada observable yang dikehendaki. Pincang ini dikira "
"sebagai jumlah sumbangan sempadan ke belakang untuk semua lokasi hingar "
"sebelum titik tersebut, ditambah dengan sumbangan sempadan ke hadapan untuk "
"semua lokasi hingar selepasnya. Pada masa ini, ini dilakukan secara seragam "
"untuk semua qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Important Note**: The point to switch from forward to backward bounds "
"depends on the learned noise rates.\n"
msgstr ""
"> **Nota Penting**: Titik untuk beralih daripada sempadan ke hadapan kepada "
"sempadan ke belakang bergantung pada kadar hingar yang dipelajari.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection-3}"
msgstr ""
"Visualkan SLC untuk pemeriksaan manual {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-"
"inspection-3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After merging the backward and tightened forward bounds, the behavior of the"
" combined SLCs becomes clear:\n"
msgstr ""
