#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"c. Execute the circuit of interest with antinoise {#c-execute-the-circuit-"
"of-interest-with-antinoise}"
msgstr ""
"c. Laksanakan litar yang diminati dengan antinoise {#c-execute-the-circuit-"
"of-interest-with-antinoise}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"c.i. Prepare template circuit by using `samplex` {#ci-prepare-template-"
"circuit-by-using-samplex}"
msgstr ""
"c.i. Sediakan template litar menggunakan `samplex` {#ci-prepare-template-"
"circuit-by-using-samplex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `samplex` is an output of the `build` method of Samplomatic, which "
"encodes all the information that is required to generate randomized "
"parameters for `template_circuit`. These are then used to set up the "
"`QuantumProgram` objects, which are in turn run on a QPU with the `Executor`"
" primitive. Each `QuantumProgram` can contain several items, which you can "
"think of as a pair of `template` and `samplex`. \n"
msgstr ""
"`samplex` adalah output kaedah `build` milik Samplomatic, yang mengekod "
"semua maklumat yang diperlukan untuk menjana parameter rawak bagi "
"`template_circuit`. Maklumat ini kemudiannya digunakan untuk menyediakan "
"objek `QuantumProgram`, yang seterusnya dijalankan pada QPU dengan primitif "
"`Executor`. Setiap `QuantumProgram` boleh mengandungi beberapa item, yang "
"boleh anda bayangkan sebagai pasangan `template` dan `samplex`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the [Hello samplomatic](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qdc-"
"challenges-2025/blob/main/day3_tutorials/Track_A/hello_samplomatic/Samplomatic%20-%20Hello%20World.ipynb)"
" tutorial for details.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat tutorial [Hello samplomatic](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qdc-"
"challenges-2025/blob/main/day3_tutorials/Track_A/hello_samplomatic/Samplomatic%20-%20Hello%20World.ipynb)"
" untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "c.ii. Set up the `QuantumProgram` {#cii-set-up-the-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "c.ii. Sediakan `QuantumProgram` {#cii-set-up-the-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"c.iii. Execute program with the `Executor` primitive {#ciii-execute-program-"
"with-the-executor-primitive}"
msgstr ""
"c.iii. Laksanakan program dengan primitif `Executor` {#ciii-execute-program-"
"with-the-executor-primitive}"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4. Post-process {#step-4-post-process}"
msgstr "Langkah 4. Pasca-proses {#step-4-post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we calculate the final expectation value of interest by using "
"`expectation_values`, we will implement a few beneficial post-processing "
"techniques to help ensure we obtain the highest-quality results possible. "
"First, we apply our [twirled readout mitigation, "
"TREX](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/error-mitigation-and-"
"suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex), which "
"accounts for any errors occurring during the readout process. Then, we fix "
"errors due to non-Markovian noise on our Heron backends by using a post-"
"selection method. This method measures active and spectator qubits, then "
"applies a slow rotation to each qubit, and then measures again. In instances"
" where the two measurements do not confirm a flipped qubit as expected, "
"these shots are discarded by applying a `mask` from the `PostSelector` "
"function. Within the mask computation, a specific strategy can be set to "
"filter based on single-qubit nodes or neighboring spectator edges, which can"
" influence both the number of shots filtered out and the quality of the "
"results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semasa kita mengira nilai jangkaan akhir yang diminati menggunakan "
"`expectation_values`, kita akan melaksanakan beberapa teknik pasca-"
"pemprosesan yang bermanfaat untuk memastikan kita mendapat hasil berkualiti "
"tinggi yang terbaik. Pertama, kita menggunakan [twirled readout mitigation, "
"TREX](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/error-mitigation-and-"
"suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex), yang "
"mengambil kira sebarang ralat yang berlaku semasa proses pembacaan. "
"Kemudian, kita memperbetulkan ralat akibat hingar bukan-Markov pada Backend "
"Heron kita menggunakan kaedah pemilihan pasca. Kaedah ini mengukur qubit "
"aktif dan spektator, kemudian mengenakan putaran perlahan kepada setiap "
"qubit, dan mengukur semula. Dalam kes di mana kedua-dua pengukuran tidak "
"mengesahkan pembalikan qubit seperti yang dijangka, shots tersebut dibuang "
"dengan menggunakan `mask` daripada fungsi `PostSelector`. Dalam pengiraan "
"mask, strategi tertentu boleh ditetapkan untuk menapis berdasarkan nod qubit"
" tunggal atau tepi spektator jiran, yang boleh mempengaruhi bilangan shots "
"yang ditapis dan kualiti hasil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From examination of the experimental results, we can directly compare the "
"behavior of different approaches: PEC, PEC combined with SLC, and the "
"baseline of unmitigated results. Some specific details to highlight:\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada pemeriksaan keputusan eksperimen, kita boleh membandingkan secara "
"terus tingkah laku pendekatan yang berbeza: PEC, PEC digabungkan dengan SLC,"
" dan garis asas hasil yang tidak dimitigasi. Beberapa butiran khusus yang "
"perlu ditonjolkan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unmitigated results remain outside the desired bias range and are unaffected"
" by sampling overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hasil yang tidak dimitigasi kekal di luar julat pincang yang dikehendaki dan"
" tidak terjejas oleh overhed pensampelan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the high sampling cost computed above (~10k), PEC alone does not "
"converge within the limits of randomization used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan kos pensampelan yang tinggi yang dikira di atas (~10k), PEC "
"sahaja tidak menumpu dalam had pengacakan yang digunakan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "PEC + SLC, in contrast, converges much more quickly.\n"
msgstr "PEC + SLC, sebaliknya, menumpu jauh lebih cepat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The error bounds also decrease significantly faster for PEC + SLC than for "
"plain PEC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sempadan ralat juga berkurangan dengan lebih ketara untuk PEC + SLC "
"berbanding PEC biasa.\n"

